% HTML Parser

document(Nodes) --> nodes(Nodes).

nodes([N|Ns]) --> node(N), nodes(Ns).
nodes([]) --> [].

node(element(Tag, Children)) --> 
    ['<'], tag_name(Tag), ['>'], 
    nodes(Children), 
    ['<', '/'], tag_name(Tag), ['>'].

node(self_closing(Tag)) --> ['<'], tag_name(Tag), ['/', '>'].
node(text(T)) --> text_chars(C), { C \= [], atom_codes(T, C) }.

tag_name(T) --> tag_chars(C), { C \= [], atom_codes(T, C) }.

tag_chars([C|Cs]) --> [C], { C >= 97, C =< 122 }, tag_chars(Cs). % a-z
tag_chars([C]) --> [C], { C >= 97, C =< 122 }.

text_chars([C|Cs]) --> [C], { C \= 60, C \= 62 }, text_chars(Cs). % not < or >
text_chars([]) --> [].\n